    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d67">

                <pb facs="0124" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.00/4–2546: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-25T09:00:00+01:00">April 25, 1946—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1964. When I accompanied the Secretary to call on Bidault this afternoon,<anchor
                        n="13" xml:id="d67-f1"/> most of the time was taken up with Bidault’s
                    opposition to trusteeship plans in connection with Tripolitania; against a
                    Russian trusteeship as well as against an international trusteeship. He repeated
                    the arguments he has advanced previously.</p>
                <pb facs="0125" n="107" xml:id="pg107"/>
                <p>In conversation on matters in general, he was more vigorous in talking against
                    Russian pretensions than he has been for some time. When I questioned him on
                    this he said that in the Cabinet meeting today (my telegram 1962 April 24<anchor
                        n="14" xml:id="d67-f2"/>) he had been given a “free hand” in foreign
                    affairs.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d67-f1" n="13" xml:id="d67-f1-content">
                <p>April 24. The Secretary arrived in Paris on April 23.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d67-f2" n="14" xml:id="d67-f2-content">
